{"id":"word:hebrew:H5159","type":"word","title":"נַחֲלָה","subtitle":"H5159 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, something inherited , i.e. (abstractly) occupancy , or (concretely) an heirloom ; generally an estate , patrimony or portion","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נַחֲלָה (H5159) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 222 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נַחֲלָה (nachălâh) means properly, something inherited , i.e. (abstractly) occupancy , or (concretely) an heirloom ; generally an estate , patrimony or portion First listed occurrence: 1Chr 16 18."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נַחֲלָה","transliteration":"nachălâh","pronunciation":"nakh-al-aw'","strong":"H5159","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5159","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["נַחֲלַ֥ת","נַחֲלָת֔/וֹ","נַחֲלָ֑ה","נַחֲלַ֛ת","נַחֲלַ֣ת"],"morphs":[["HNcfsa",37],["HNcfsc",34],["HNcfsc/Sp3ms",31],["HR/Ncfsa",28],["HNcfsc/Sp3mp",15],["HNcfsc/Sp2ms",9],["HNcfsc/Sp1cs",8],["HR/Ncfsc",7],["HC/Ncfsa",7],["HR/Ncfsc/Sp3ms",6]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, something inherited , i.e. (abstractly) occupancy , or (concretely) an heirloom ; generally an estate , patrimony or portion","usage":"heritage, to inherit, inheritance, possession. Compare 5158 .","full":"H5159. nachalah נַחֲלָה 224 noun feminine possession, property, inheritance (originally gift ; Late Hebrew = Biblical Hebrew); — ׳נ Num 18:23 +; נַחֲלָת Psa 16:6 (Ges § 90g ), read נַחֲלָתִי Ew SS We Kö ii. 1, 425 ; construct נַחֲלַת Josh 13:23 ; suffix נַחֲלָתִי Ruth 4:6 ; נַחֲלַתְכֶם Psa 105:11 ; plural נְחָלוֺת Isa 49:8 , נְחָלֹת Josh 19:51 ; 1 property: a. in Canaan given by ׳י to Israel, ישׂראל נחלת Judg 20:6 ; ׳נ יעקב Isa 58:14 , especially נַחֲלָה לְךָ נֹתֵן אֲשֶׁר Deut 4:21 ; 15:4 ; 19:10 ; 20:16 ; Deuteronomy 21:28; 24:4 ; 25:19 ; 26:1 (all D); עמי את הנחלתי אשׁר הנחלה Jer 12:14 . b. distributive among tribes: נ ׳נתן לְ Num 16:14 ; 36:2 ; Josh 14:3 (restore לְ ), 17:4 , 14 ; 19:49 (all P); לנ ׳נתן לְ Deut 29:7 ; Josh 11:23 ; 14:13 (all D 2 ); נחלה נָָֽחֲלוּ 17:6 (J); בּנ ׳תֵּחָלֵק Num 26:53 , 56 (P); בּנחלה נפל 34:2 (P), Judg 18:1 ; Ezek 47:22 ; בנ ׳הפיל Josh 13:6 ; 23:4 (D 2 ), Ezek 45:1 ; 47:22 , also 47:22 (Co reads ב for מ ). c. nations as possession of the people , Psa 111:6 ; of the king 2:8 . d. Levites have no property in the land Num 18:23-24 , Deut 10:9 ; 12:12 ; their possession is ׳י Num 18:20 (P); ׳י נחלתו הוּא Deut 10:9 ; 18:2 ; Josh 13:14 , 33 (all D); the tithes Num 18:21 , 24 , 26 (P). e. ׳י takes Israel as his property, 1Sam 10:1 ; 1Kin 8:53 ; 2Kin 21:14 ; Isa 19:25 ; Micah 7:18 ; Psa 33:12 ; 68:10 ; 106:5 ; נחלה עם Deut 4:20 (D 2 ); וְנַחֲלָֽתְךָ עַמְּךָ 9:26 , 29 (D), 1Kin 8:51 ; || עַם Isa 47:6 ; Joel 2:17 ; Joel 4:2; Micah 7:14 ; Psa 28:9 ; 78:62 ; 78:71 ; 94:5 ; 94:14 ; 106:40 ; י ׳נחלת 1Sam 26:19 ; 2Sam 20:19 ; 21:3 ; ׳נ אלהים 14:16 ; נ חבל ׳יעקב Deut 32:9 ; נ ׳שׁבט Jer 10:16 = 51:19 , Psa 74:2 ; נ ׳שׁבטי Isa 63:17 ; also, the holy mountain Exod 15:17 (song), temple Jer 12:7 ; Psa 79:1 , land Jer 2:7 ; 12:8-9 , 16:18 ; 50:11 . 2 portion, share: a. assigned by God , Isa 54:17 ; Psa 37:18 ; 127:3 ; elsewhere || חֵלֶק Job 20:29 ; 27:13 ; 31:2 . b. by choice , || נ ׳לא ישׁי בבן לנו חֵלֶק, 2Sam 20:1 we have no share in the son of Jesse = 1Kin 12:16 2Chr 10:16 . 3 inheritance (45 t.) אָבִּינוּ בְּבֵית וְנַחֲלָה חֵלֶק Gen 31:14 (E) portion or inheritance in the house of our father ; נ ׳העביר לְ Num 27:7-8 , (P) cause the inheritance to pass unto ; נ ׳נתן לְ 27:9-10 , 11 (P), Job 42:15 ; אבות נחלת Num 36:3 , 8 ; 1Kin 21:3-4 , Prov 19:14 ; ׳נ תהיה לבניו Ezek 46:16 .","rootNote":"from 5157 (in its usual sense);","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 16 18","keyReferences":["1Chr 16 18","1Kgs 8 36","1Kgs 8 51","1Kgs 8 53","1Kgs 12 16","1Kgs 21 3","1Kgs 21 4","1Sam 10 1"],"related":{"peo